      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `NullReader_ESTest_test12.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-io/auto/testcases/NullReader_ESTest/NullReader_ESTest_test12.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It creates a `NullReader` with size 0, reads from it (which triggers EOF), then verifies that `skip()` throws `IOException` because we're past EOF. Let me write an improved, more understandable version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test adds a named constant `LARGE_SKIP_AMOUNT` for the magic number, renames the test method to `test_skipAfterEofThrowsIOException` to clearly express intent, uses descriptive variable names (`reader`, `buffer`), and adds a comment explaining why the first `read()` call is needed before the skip."
    }
